---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
// name, lon, lat, what, kind, label side
const places = [
  ['Hammerstein (Czarne)', 16.94, 53.68, 'Sally Leibholz born 1847. Georg born 1884 — which is why he cannot be Jacob’s brother', 'leib', 'w'],
  ['Szubin (Schubin)', 17.74, 53.00, 'Sally married Friederike 1874. Samuel 1877, Jacob 1884, Oskar 1887 all born here', 'leib', 'e'],
  ['Allenstein (Olsztyn)', 20.48, 53.78, 'Joachim Luwinski born 1865. A Landwirt', 'luw', 'e'],
  ['Sauerbaum, Kreis Rössel', 21.15, 54.35, 'Johanna Thimm born 1871; Auguste born 1893', 'luw', 'e'],
  ['Berlin', 13.40, 52.52, 'Kurt born 1912. Four addresses: Meraner Str. 2, Kommandantenstr. 29, Waghäuseler Str. 9/10, Michaelkirchstr. 26', 'both', 'w'],
  ['Sommerfeld', 12.98, 52.95, 'Where Siegfried was hidden, January 1943 to April 1945', 'luw', 'w'],
  ['Łódź', 19.46, 51.76, 'Georg and Lydia, in the ghetto from 1 November 1941', 'end', 'e'],
  ['Chełmno (Kulmhof)', 18.72, 52.15, 'Georg and Lydia, 13 May 1942', 'end', 'e'],
  ['Theresienstadt', 14.15, 50.51, 'Oskar, 17 March 1943', 'end', 'w'],
  ['Auschwitz', 19.20, 50.03, 'Jacob 26 Feb 1943 · Samuel 10 Apr 1943 · Oskar 16 Oct 1944', 'end', 'e'],
  ['Kraichtal', 8.72, 49.14, 'Auguste died 1975', 'luw', 'w'],
  ['Eixo, Aveiro', -8.55, 40.62, 'Augusto Pereira de Figueiredo baptised 1883 — candidate only', 'fig', 'e'],
  ['Porto', -8.61, 41.35, 'Ivone died and was buried', 'fig', 'e'],
  ['Amadora, Oeiras', -9.23, 38.76, 'Augusto died 21 August 1954', 'fig', 'e'],
];
const world = [
  ['Berlin', 13.40, 52.52, 'both', 'e'],
  ['Lisbon / Porto', -8.61, 41.15, 'fig', 'e'],
  ['Lourenço Marques', 32.58, -25.97, 'fig', 'e'],
  ['Johannesburg', 28.05, -26.20, 'both', 'w'],
];
const colour = { leib: 'var(--disp)', luw: 'var(--inf)', fig: 'var(--doc)', end: 'var(--accent)', both: 'var(--ink)' };
// Europe panel
const EW = 1000, EH = 460;
const ex = l => ((l + 12) / 36) * EW;
const ey = l => ((56.5 - l) / 19) * EH;
// World panel
const WW = 1000, WH = 520;
const wx = l => ((l + 20) / 62) * WW;
const wy = l => ((60 - l) / 92) * WH;
---
<Base title="Atlas"
  subtitle="Every place this archive can put a date to"
  lede="It runs from a Pomeranian market town to the Indian Ocean and back to the Atlantic, and the shape of it is the twentieth century.">

  <h2>Europe</h2>
  <div class="scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${EW} ${EH}`} width="100%" role="img" aria-label="The European places"
         style="min-width:54rem;background:var(--panel);display:block">
      <path d={`M${ex(17.74)},${ey(53.00)} L${ex(13.40)},${ey(52.52)}`} stroke="var(--disp)" stroke-width="2.5" opacity=".6" fill="none" />
      <path d={`M${ex(20.48)},${ey(53.78)} L${ex(13.40)},${ey(52.52)}`} stroke="var(--inf)" stroke-width="2.5" opacity=".6" fill="none" />
      <path d={`M${ex(13.40)},${ey(52.52)} L${ex(19.46)},${ey(51.76)} L${ex(18.72)},${ey(52.15)}`} stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" opacity=".85" fill="none" />
      <path d={`M${ex(13.40)},${ey(52.52)} L${ex(19.20)},${ey(50.03)}`} stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" opacity=".85" fill="none" />
      <path d={`M${ex(13.40)},${ey(52.52)} L${ex(14.15)},${ey(50.51)} L${ex(19.20)},${ey(50.03)}`} stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 4" opacity=".7" fill="none" />
      {places.map(([n, lo, la, , k, side]) => (
        <circle cx={ex(lo)} cy={ey(la)} r={k === 'end' ? 7 : 5.5} fill={colour[k]} stroke="var(--panel)" stroke-width="2" />
      ))}
      {places.map(([n, lo, la, , k, side]) => (
        <text x={ex(lo) + (side === 'w' ? -11 : 11)} y={ey(la) + 4}
              text-anchor={side === 'w' ? 'end' : 'start'} font-size="13" fill="var(--ink-soft)"
              font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">{n}</text>
      ))}
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">
    Red lines are the deportations. The dashed one is Oskar, who went to Theresienstadt first and
    reached Auschwitz nineteen months later.
  </p>

  <h2>And the two long journeys</h2>
  <div class="scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${WW} ${WH}`} width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Berlin to Johannesburg, Lourenço Marques to Johannesburg to Porto"
         style="min-width:44rem;background:var(--panel);display:block">
      <path d={`M${wx(13.40)},${wy(52.52)} L${wx(28.05)},${wy(-26.20)}`} stroke="var(--ink-faint)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="8 6" fill="none" />
      <path d={`M${wx(32.58)},${wy(-25.97)} L${wx(28.05)},${wy(-26.20)}`} stroke="var(--doc)" stroke-width="3" fill="none" />
      <path d={`M${wx(28.05)},${wy(-26.20)} L${wx(-8.61)},${wy(41.15)}`} stroke="var(--doc)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 5" fill="none" opacity=".75" />
      {world.map(([n, lo, la, k, side]) => (
        <circle cx={wx(lo)} cy={wy(la)} r="7" fill={colour[k]} stroke="var(--panel)" stroke-width="2" />
      ))}
      {world.map(([n, lo, la, k, side]) => (
        <text x={wx(lo) + (side === 'w' ? -12 : 12)} y={wy(la) + 4}
              text-anchor={side === 'w' ? 'end' : 'start'} font-size="14" fill="var(--ink-soft)"
              font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">{n}</text>
      ))}
      <text x={wx(13.4) + 120} y={wy(20)} font-size="13" fill="var(--ink-faint)" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">Kurt, 1933</text>
      <text x={wx(32.58) - 6} y={wy(-25.97) + 26} font-size="13" fill="var(--doc)" text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">Ivone — 400 miles of railway</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">
    A plain equirectangular frame: longitude and latitude are true, nothing else about it is meant
    to be. The dashed line south is 1933. The dashed line north is Ivone, at the end.
  </p>

  <h2>The places, with what happened at them</h2>
  <div class="scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Place</th><th>What happened</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {places.map(([n, , , what, k]) => (
        <tr><td><strong style={`color:${colour[k]}`}>{n}</strong></td><td class="small">{what}</td></tr>
      ))}
      <tr><td><strong style={`color:${colour.fig}`}>Lourenço Marques (Maputo)</strong></td><td class="small">Ivone Mota Figueiredo born 4 March 1924. Henrique born 1941</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong style={`color:${colour.both}`}>Johannesburg</strong></td><td class="small">Kurt from 1933. Married 1948. Kurt buried 1968 — Westpark, block L, grave 211</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>What the shape of it says</h2>
  <p>
    Two families that began four hundred kilometres apart — Jewish at Szubin, Catholic at Allenstein
    — converge on <strong>one city</strong>, and inside Berlin on <strong>four streets</strong>. Then
    the line breaks in two directions at once. One son goes eight thousand kilometres south in 1933
    and lives. His father, his uncles and his aunt go three hundred kilometres east between 1941 and
    1944, and do not.
  </p>
  <p>
    The other half of the map has nothing to do with any of it.
    <strong>Lourenço Marques to Johannesburg</strong> is a railway line and four hundred miles; it is
    how Ivone arrived, and it is the only reason these two halves are on one page. She ended at
    <strong>Porto</strong>, which nobody else in this archive ever saw.
  </p>
</Base>
